    "updated_at": "2025-08-07T20:51:20Z",
    "body": "@bkardell, thanks. That makes it clearer.\n\n<em>I</em> want to be able to consistently annotate with a MIME type, such that a consumer can recognise a language: your first option. I didn't know of a more extensible way to annotate these, but that may be because I'm unfamiliar with some of the use cases you've proposed.\n\nTangentially, <em>I</em> would <em>like</em> to see this as a feature of the browser, since text editors do it so damn well. However, I recognise that that's outside the scope of this: it's a dicussion for Bugzilla. Regardless, the second use case is dependent upon the first.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
